## Data

This repository contains **derived** data in `profiles/`, `data/golden/` and
`data/offline_seed.json`. It is not relicensed by the MIT grant above. Each
source keeps its own terms, and the required attribution is reproduced here and
in full in [`docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`](docs/DATA_SOURCES.md).

### Brønnøysundregistrene — Enhetsregisteret and Regnskapsregisteret

Open data under the **Norwegian Licence for Open Government Data (NLOD) 2.0**.
The attribution string required by that licence is:

> Inneholder data under norsk lisens for offentlige data (NLOD) tilgjengeliggjort
> av Brønnøysundregistrene.

(Translation: "Contains data under the Norwegian licence for Open Government
Data (NLOD), made available by the Brønnøysund Register Centre.")

Sources:

- Enhetsregisteret — <https://data.brreg.no/enhetsregisteret/api>
- Regnskapsregisteret — <https://data.brreg.no/regnskapsregisteret>

### GLEIF

Legal Entity Identifier records from the Global LEI Foundation, published under
**CC0 1.0 Universal** (public domain dedication).
<https://www.gleif.org/en/lei-data/gleif-api>

### Wikidata

Structured data from Wikidata, published under **CC0 1.0 Universal**.
<https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Wikidata:Data_access>

### Company websites

Quoted text is reproduced verbatim and in short excerpts only, with the source
URL and retrieval date recorded on every fact, for the purpose of attribution
and verification. No page is crawled that `robots.txt` disallows.

## Personal data

The profiles describe **organisations, not people**. Sole traders (`ENK`) are
natural persons, so the web-enrichment layer is skipped for those entities
entirely (`is_organisational_contact()` in `src/extract_rules.py`) rather than
filtered afterwards. Only role-based mailboxes and switchboard numbers are
harvested, and the gap-filling schema has no field for a named individual. See
[`docs/DATA_SOURCES.md`](docs/DATA_SOURCES.md) for the full policy.
